Sūrya.

The Sun.

And its fruit is:

Sthiti-sāmarthya.

The capacity to sustain.

Now here’s the lovely correspondence.

Creation.

Maintenance.

Two cosmic activities.

And the Moon and Sun are contemplated as divine expressions through which these powers become manifest.

Now, we’ve discussed seven forms.

Earth.

Water.

Wind.

Fire.

Space.

Moon.

Sun.

One remains.

And it’s the most important of all.

Self — non-difference
