Non-difference.

Now, that’s absolutely magnificent.

Because the entire purpose of these practices is the recognition that there is no ultimate separation between the individual and supreme consciousness.

And the eighth form is precisely the Self.

Not another external object.

Not another cosmic element.

The very principle of subjectivity.

And through this, the eightfold practice culminates in the recognition of non-difference.

Now, notice the progression.

We began with concrete forms.

Earth.

Water.

Wind.

Fire.

Then space.

Then the great celestial powers.

And finally the Self.

And the entire range is understood through mantra and identification with Parameśvara.

The world that appeared external becomes a means of recognising the consciousness in which externality itself appears.

But Abhinavagupta isn’t finished.

Because apparently there’s a special version of this bath.

For the vīras.

The tantric heroes.

And let me tell you something.

These lads aren’t mucking about.

