But with reference to the hero, there’s a special variation.

And then he gives us another eightfold list.

Only this time, the ordinary forms have been transformed.

First:

Raṇareṇu.

The dust of battle.

Or dust associated with heroic activity.

Now that’s quite a departure from our previous discussion of ordinary earth.

Instead of simply taking the ground as the supporting form, we encounter dust marked by the world of the vīra.

Second:

Vīrāmbhas.

The water of the hero.

